update public.government_schemes
set summary_en='Punjab Government housing initiative for low-income households. The official SMU page describes affordable housing units and interest-free construction loans up to PKR 1.5 million for eligible plot owners. The current application intake and deadline must still be checked on the official portal.',
summary_ur='کم آمدن گھرانوں کے لیے حکومتِ پنجاب کا رہائشی پروگرام۔ سرکاری SMU صفحہ رہائشی یونٹس اور اہل پلاٹ مالکان کے لیے 15 لاکھ روپے تک بلاسود تعمیراتی قرض کا ذکر کرتا ہے۔ موجودہ درخواستوں اور آخری تاریخ کی تصدیق سرکاری پورٹل سے کریں۔',
benefit_details='The official Punjab SMU page describes a target of 100,000 affordable houses/apartments across Punjab over four and a half years, through several routes: 10,000 units on state land; 20,000 affordable units in private housing schemes with a government subsidy of PKR 1 million per unit and a five-year instalment plan for the allottee; and 70,000 interest-free construction loans of up to PKR 1.5 million for eligible plot owners, with a seven-year tenure and monthly instalments. These are different programme routes; the route available to an applicant depends on the official programme process.',
eligibility_text='The official page lists permanent Punjab residence by CNIC (applicant or a family member); sole ownership and possession of a residential plot up to 5 marla in urban areas or 10 marla in rural areas for the construction-loan route; no criminal record for specified serious offences; and no default on a loan from a bank or financial institution. Other housing routes may have different conditions. Check the live portal for the exact route-specific criteria.',
fees_and_repayment='For the construction-loan route, the official page states interest-free financing up to PKR 1.5 million over seven years with monthly instalments. For the private-scheme affordable-housing route, the page states a PKR 1 million government subsidy per unit, a down payment by the allottee and a five-year instalment plan. No current application fee is confirmed in the source page reviewed. Confirm the current route and terms on the official portal.',
application_steps='Open the official ACAG portal and read the current registration instructions. The SMU page still refers to there being no announced last date in 2025; that is not a valid 2026 deadline. Confirm that the relevant route is currently accepting applications before submitting information. Hello Sadiqabad does not collect applications.',
verified_at=now(),next_review_at=now()+interval '7 days',updated_at=now()
where slug='apni-chhat-apna-ghar';

update public.government_schemes
set official_apply_url='https://pmyp.gov.pk/',
application_steps='The PID announcement dated 10 November 2026 says applicants can use the Prime Minister’s Digital Youth Hub at pmyp.gov.pk or the PMYP mobile app. The separate PMYB&ALS information portal reviewed still displays the original three tiers and its online application link; confirm the current form route and Tier 4 implementation through the official hub / participating bank before applying. No agent or recommendation is required; banks decide applications on merit. Never upload identity or supporting documents to Hello Sadiqabad or share them in chat.',
verified_at=now(),next_review_at=now()+interval '7 days',updated_at=now()
where slug='prime-minister-youth-business-agriculture-loan';

update public.government_schemes
set source_document_url='https://hunarmand.bisp.gov.pk/doc/Hunarmand_english.pdf',
eligibility_text='The current official portal states that applicants must be registered in the BISP Dynamic Registry, have at least Matric education, be aged 18–40, and only one person per family may register. An older official guide PDF lists first-phase districts as Lahore, Karachi, Peshawar, Quetta, Islamabad, Rawalpindi, Gilgit and Muzaffarabad; it does not list Rahim Yar Khan / Sadiqabad. That guide may not reflect the current phase, so confirm current district coverage and course availability on the portal before travelling. Registration does not guarantee selection.',
application_steps='Register only through the official Benazir Hunarmand portal or follow its instructions for the nearest Tehsil Office. The portal says registration is reviewed and eligible applicants are selected. An older official guide PDF lists only eight first-phase districts and does not include Rahim Yar Khan / Sadiqabad; check the current district list with BISP before travelling.',
verified_at=now(),next_review_at=now()+interval '7 days',updated_at=now()
where slug='benazir-hunarmand-programme';